QEMU rollback boot rehearsal on a disposable qcow2 copy-on-write overlay; no physical drive attached.

Procedure: copied the valid target production UKI to gentoo-fallback.efi, replaced gentoo-production.efi with an intentionally invalid stub, then called the project's rollback_production_uki() to restore production from fallback. The restored images matched SHA-256 5c3f7b92011e586eb22fa202459a2d26c79103f4ae35dd3d294c35893ff4d9a5. The project writer regenerated the explicit production/fallback entries and loader.conf default gentoo-production with timeout 5.

OVMF/QEMU then booted the restored overlay. It reached the expected encrypted-root device and cryptsetup passphrase prompt. No passphrase was entered because the disposable test key had been removed. QMP reported SHUTDOWN (host-qmp-quit), QEMU exited 0. The ESP passed fsck.vfat -n before and after boot; both UKI files still had the same SHA-256 after boot. qemu-img check reported no errors.

This rehearses the rollback function and boot of the restored image. It does not invoke the guarded kernel-rollback CLI inside Gentoo; its OS, mount, and disk-serial guards are covered by separate temporary-EFI CLI integration tests. It also does not repeat LUKS unlock/login.

